PATCH 643: preserve original effects BYTE state and neighboring code (board:0003).

Original op68 dispatches directly to76fd. Its first instruction A2 E1 77 00 00
stores AL into one BYTE at77e1. The ready tests at7719/773e are80 3D E0 77
00 00 01: CMP BYTE[77e0],1. Both generated DWORD accessors violate that
contract. The mode store zeros actual77e2's C6 05 E0 instruction prefix;
the ready read includes mode2 and the following code bytes, so ready1 fails
the comparison and never calls the existing23ec initial mixer.

tools/oracle/effects_mode_case.json proves the actual ready0/ready1 mode2
entries and full original fetched BYTE instructions. The ready1 module and
DMA fields at76fd/138d equal initial_mixer_call_case.json's before/after
fields, verified against paging-aware original whole-RAM snapshots. Reuse
that regression's one-MiB module, 2048-byte DMA fixture, actual ordered76fd,
23ec,2630 and24c8 bodies, and device-entry observer. No initializer result
is supplied. Parent123547c fails four Native/WASM cases: ready0 corrupts
77e2..77e4; ready1 omits required138d entry. With only these two BYTE
accessors corrected, complete module/DMA output matches on both targets.

This fixes shared storage width only. Production op68 is not yet wired;
76fd's return/full GP,23ec's register ABI, actual138d device/IF/IRQ work,
other effects modes, CPU time and final mixed PCM remain open. The poison
second C argument is unused on these active0 paths and proves no ABI.
